{number: 49}
{title: O Happy Day That Fixed My Choice}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] O happy day that fixed my choice
On Thee, my Savior [G7] and my [C] God!
Well may this glowing heart rejoice,
And tell its raptures [G7] all a-[C] broad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Happy day, happy day,
When Jesus washed my [G7] sins a-[C] way!
He [G7] taught me how to watch and pray,
And live re-[C] joicing ev'ry day;
[C] Happy day, happy day,
When Jesus washed my [G7] sins a-[C] way!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
'Tis [C] done-the great transaction's done;
I am my Lord's, and [G7] He is [C] mine;
He drew me, and I followed on,
Rejoiced to own the [G7] call di-[C] vine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Now [C] rest, my long-divided heart;
Fixed on this blissful [G7] center, [C] rest;
Here have I found a nobler part,
Here heav’nly pleasures [G7] fill my [C] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
High [C] heav’n that hears the solemn vows,
That vow renewed shall [G7] daily [C] hear;
Till in life’s latest hour I bow,
And bless in death, a [G7] bond so [C] dear.
{end_of_verse}
